      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-17_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>GOOD NEWS FOR LADIES.</head>
        <p>GOOD NEWS FOR LADIES.</p>
        <p>A LADY, the daugh rof a late eminent physician, will be 11 pleased to forward full particularb (on receipt of a stamped directed envelope) of a Certs.f.n Cure for all forms ef Irreg.tlarities. no matter how caused or how long standing The Remedy causes no Pain, Nausea, or Prostration what ever.</p>
        <p>MADAME DOUGLAS, 127, Gaisford-street, London, N.W A Positive Cure Guaranteed.</p>
        <p>Houma sto 9 p.m.. on TUESDAYS, THURSDAYS, or by appointment. Name this paper</p>
        <p>*rbolagtir</p>
        <p>STOP FOR PARRY'S GREAT FURNITURE SALE. Catalogoo now ready, post free on application. Address 20, DOWNING-STREt T. MANCHESTER. Mahogany Sofa. Gent's and Ladles' Easy and 4 small Chairs sft. Sideboard with massive plate-glass back, brown oak 2 2 Stu f back Dining-room Fulte in saddlebags. quite new 5 5 Solid Ros.wood Drawing-room Smite of 9 pieces, in hair</p>
        <p>Solid Walnut Dining-room suite of nine pieces. real - morocco</p>
        <p>Aft. Solul Mahogany Dresser, with brass handles 2 16 61t. Extending Dining Tdde, with p,tent screw Large Mahogany Wardrobe, with bevelled plate centre door Pair of Mahogany .9tands, fixed glass and rnarole slab, on castors 1 18 4ft. Enclosed Washstani and D.easing Table. with swing glass 51t. 2-door wardrobe, three chairs and the lot Handsome 7ft. Burr Walnut P.edroom Suite cost 90gs 29 0 flask rwld limes Fali-siar Bedsteads, and Mattress corn- , pl.*</p>
        <p>KEATING'S COUGH LOZENGES.</p>
        <p>THE CREWE AND DISTRICT LOAN Co., (Est. 1`,89). 32, CEMETERY-ROAD, CREWh.</p>
        <p>ADVANCES CASH from £5 upwards on the shortest notice, in town or country, male or female, upon simple promissory notes, on Mortgage of Furniture, Trade and Farm Stock, Crops, Plants, itc. Without removal. Also on deeds reversions, stocks, shares and inerchtndise of every descrip tion, repayable by easy instalments. Distance no object Anyone requiring money will do well, before applying else where or paving fees to think of this •• Surely I can dc better with a firm who have teen established in Cheshire many years,and devoting themselves to this class of business than I can with sacalled private money lf.-nders or agents with small means. Good borrowers can obtain money here on reasonable terms and quickly. Write or call for prospectus. W. JACKSON. Manager.</p>
        <p>DINING-ROOM FURNITURE. Lot 50. Second-hand Spanish Mahogany Dining-room Suite, in Morocco, handsomely carved for £B. Lot 51 t•econd-hand American Wa.nut Dining-room Suite In leather, £4 15s. Lot 52: Seoond-hand Brown Oak Dining-room Suite, in velvet, 5 guineas. Lot 53. An e•Arserclinary Massive Dining-room Suite, in Spanish Mahogany, consisting of a spoon-back Suite, of Couch. !wo Easy Chairs, and six Single Chairs, upholstered in Morocco, Magnificent Spanish Mahogany Sideboard to match, with lofty plate-glass back, most beautifully carved in good preservation. 10ft. Dl in.,-table on massive carved sup- ports. This lot is worth to-day 2100 and oast over 2200 wben new, and will be sold a bargain or 240. Lot 54. Fine old Spanish Sideboard, 7ft. 61n. long, in Spanish mahogany, coat £7O. Lot 56. Second hand Dining-room Suite complete, with Sideboard, Tab.e. and Overmantel. the suite upholstered in Morocco. Cost £B6. Price ssi guineas. Lot 57. Good Second-hand Dining-room Suite, of nine pieces, splendid Sideboard and Dining Table to seat 10 per- sons, together with the Overmantel. Our price for quick sale 15 guineas. Lot 58. Magnificent Pollard Oak Dining-room Suite, suit- able for a nobleman. This Furniture is second-hand, but it Is quite equal to new, havind been entirely re-upholstered in Morocco; it is in beautifulcondition,and spotless throughout. The design is original, and is by a celebrated maker. The Sideboard is 7ft long, palatial in size, and beautiful in de- sign ; the wood Is the very finest figured Pollard Oak. The carving is executed In fine has relief,and is a work of art. The Suite is by Taylor and Whitfield ; the carving alone must have cost a fabulous sum. tontii:4B of very beautiful Coach. pair of Easy Chairs end six Single Chairs. We can proviie 12 Single Chairs if necessary. The Dining Table is latt long and matches the rest of the Furniture. We have not the slightest hesitation in ricclaring that this Furniture is worth £5OO. Our price for the lot is £2OO. N.B.—lt will be seen by the let 58 we have just described that W 0 SL nY'S must have a very extensive stock. We have just described three pieces of Furniture for £2OO, and while in Lot 57 we give a lot for Diningroom for 15 guineas, show- ing what a wide and Extt-usive Stock Worsiev's have on show. We have over 100 complete Diningroom Suites on show, besides scores of odd Sideboards and odd Dining Tables.</p>
        <p>DRAWING-ROOM FURNITURE. In this Department we have perhaps the finest selec- tion of Furniture to be seen in any boase in the country. It is very difficult to select out of the bargains on view in this room a few that will convey a fair idea of their ma2nifi- cence and quality in this short paragraph ; there are such a quantity of them. We have over 's_oo Drawing-room Suites on show in every variety of colour and shade of upholstery. We give one or two examp'es : Lot 215. Very exquisitely pretty and unique Chippendale Drawing-room nuite for £l2. perhlps the greatest marvel of any barktin that has been offered ; it is quite sufficient to day that this Suite is beautifully inlaid and covered in the finest silk tapestry. It is a second-hand suite which has been re covered and re•polished, and entirely reuov-tted, and is now entirely equal to new. It would undoubtedly compare favourably with anything that is being offered for £25 and £33 eleswhere. We have the Cabinet to match at the same price, £l2. This is just as beautifully made, contains numerous shelves for bric-a-brac, and splendidly fitted with bevel plates ; there is also an t)vermantel, which matches. for 3 guineas. two Occasional Tables at 18s, each, a Music Cabinet for £2 155., and Lady's Writing Table for £3 10s• alto2ether forming the prettiest collection of Chippendale furnit•tre which has ever been on show at the price. Lots 310 to 330. A tine Collection of 20 Second-hand Cabi- nets and Chiffoniers from £2 10s. up to £lO. These have been marked exceedingly low to clear, and are of the good old-fashioned make. Everyone of these are second-hand. Lots 351 to 365 Fourteen Wonderfully Cheap Overmantels, second-hand. Some of these cost as much as £2O, We shall offer them from 30s. to £5.</p>
        <p>Lot 366. SPECIAL BARGAIN. The Prettiest. Best, and Cheapest Drawing-room Suite ever offered. This Suite is of exceptional merit ; it consists of the sweetest designed Settee, and pair of Easy Chairs, two exquisite Occasional Chairs,and two beautiful Single Chairs. The whole is very prettily in- laid w,th ivory, met upholstered in silk tapestry ; well worth 255. per yard. he Cab Wet to match is of a design both weird and pesuliar ;curious littla columns with niches ior the display of china,grotesque little cupboards fitted with bevelled crystals. speci a cover, and of peculiar shape for five o'clock tea service; two of the trickiest little tables imaginable, a peculiar and beautiful little Overmantel to match the lot. design of wlsich is just as grotesque and curious as the rest of Furniture. This is the kind of Suite that lades fall in love with wherever it is seen. Our price for the lot 24 guineas, REDROOM FURNITURg. woIiSLICY'S have the Biggest Show of Bedroom Furni- ture of anyone in the United Kingdom. We are quite aware that most Houses lay claim to having the Biggest Stock, but we challenge any intending purchaser to compare by inspec- tion the Enormous stock of Bedroom Furniture at WOES- LEY'S with that of any other House in the Kingdom. We have over 300 Bedroom Suites on show. We have just com- pleted another contract for 300 lEdroom Suites for our stock, and we have in pro ess of manufacture.orders with manufac- turers of bedsteads which shall bring our stock to little short of 1,0:.-0 i-edsteads. Out of this varied collection we select a few sample bargains only. SPECIAL NOT ICH. You might hear a remark that it is very seldom son visit WORsLEY'S but that you can pick up such a bargain that more than repays the trouble of your 'visit. Lot 789. A Ma,gnificent Pollard nak BEDROOM SUITE will be sold a bargain to, £l2O which originally cost £5OO. This is the finest bedroom suite in Manchester. Lot 792. A Very Handsome Bedroom Suite, smaller in size, suitable for a young lady's bedroom, exquisitely pretty, of a classical design, and the best workmanship throughout; price 10 guineas. We have a tremendous Stock of Odd Wardrobss, mall kind of woods. We have Wardrobes, 6ft. long, enamelled woods, toritaining numerous drawers. tray shelves, and hanging compartments ; these run from £2 up to £6 Les. We have next a big co lection of Washstands and Dressing- tables in mahogsny, walnut oak, and enamelled woods. We can do a magnificent Pair of Mahogany Stands for £3 10s. We have Walnut Stands, the pair complete, for £2 15s and upwa els. We have Oren Stands from 12s 6d. But if you want a bargain, no matter whether you wish to give £5 or £5O. you c.in meet weth what you require at WOUSL • Y'S. Lot 796. The Drest lug Table and Washstand to match, Sit; fine, handsome, massive. and richly figured in the wood. This is a very bold and large pair of Che Val Stands, price £25. The same could not be obtained for £f:o else- where.</p>
        <p>We cannot trespass on the spaee of this paper to any greater extent. We shall issues new advertisement, with anew list next week. Don't forget that we are quite willing to show you all our bargains, whet her you buy or not, and that if you do purchase and do not require immediate delivery we will store them free of charge.</p>
        <p>BEDSTKADS and BEDDING. Lot 1,101. MAgnificent Second-hand Solid Brass B.dsteads, beautifully chased, splendid design; cost £2O, for £3 10s. _ _</p>
        <p>Lot 1,105. Very handsome Solid Brass Persian Bedstead. massive pillars ; cost £3O, tor 10 guineas. Lot 1,107. Job lot of Second-hand Persian Bedsteads to be sold cheat), from 153 to 30s. Lot 1,141. Fit y cond-hand Fr, nch Bedsteads to be cleared out at any price. from 4s 6d to lOs 6d. Lot 1,192. A 'Job lot, all Solid Brass Reclete.,ds, slightly soiled, from 25s to £3 10s.</p>
        <p>BRASt, FENDERS and BRASS: ES, Lot 1,786. Magnificent Suite of Solid Brass Fender, Pair of magnificent Dogs, and Patent Stop : all second-hand; equal to new; cost £25 ; tor £3 10s. Lot 1,789. Very hani.some Second-hand Brass Curl), Dogs, and Brasses ; coat £lO for 358 Lot 1.790. Elegant Ni w Fire Suite, consisting of heantifal chased fender, pair of very handsome dogs. and set of exquis- ite fire brasses, all guite new designs. The suite complete for 2 guineas, Lot 1,791. Very good Solid Brass and Enamelled Suite of Fender, Brasses, and Dogs, for 218 ;honestly worth £4. Lot 1,792 Very Heavy Solid Brass Fender, second-hand. cost £8; 3 's Lot 1,793. New Solid Brass Fire Suite,consisting of fender, brasses, and dogs: splendid design, for 19s 6rl Lot 1,794 Job Lot of Soiled Fenders, from 4s 6d to a-guinea. Some ot these loaders are worth several poonds•</p>
        <p>w. H. Ave,RsLY, " THE PANTHEON," , GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER. AU City-road Cats Pass Buitinees Hours, WORt LEY'S. 9to 7.</p>
      </div>
