        <p>Sir,—Great praise is due to your Patent Ha!sun of Honey, and pirticularly amongst the aged. I have not the least doubt that when this hard weither breaks,thot the men can resu lie work again, you will receive nuns bars of orders. There are a great number here suffering from Coughs, Colds, and Chest Affrictions. I will not be without a bottle of it in the house henceforth.—Yours faithfullyaurrnun FletszY,2,Clifton Villaq,Plevna Road, Hampton, Middlesex. February 12th, 1895.</p>
